# AI Companion Database System with Speech-to-Speech Modulation

This plan outlines the architecture, database schema, and Python implementation of a premium, modular SQLite database tailored specifically for an AI Companion application. The system will store conversation history (inputs and responses), voice profiles, and detailed metrics for speech-to-speech voice modulation.

## Proposed Architecture

```mermaid
erDiagram
    SESSIONS ||--o{ MESSAGES : "contains"
    MESSAGES ||--o| SPEECH_MODULATION_LOGS : "logs modulation for"
    VOICE_PROFILES ||--o{ SPEECH_MODULATION_LOGS : "uses profile"

    SESSIONS {
        string session_id PK
        string companion_name
        string summary
        datetime created_at
        datetime updated_at
    }

    MESSAGES {
        string message_id PK
        string session_id FK
        string sender "user | companion"
        string text_content
        string audio_path
        blob audio_blob
        int latency_ms
        datetime created_at
    }

    VOICE_PROFILES {
        string profile_id PK
        string name "unique name"
        float pitch_shift "pitch shifting in semitones"
        float speed_rate "speed rate multiplier"
        float volume_gain "gain in dB"
        string voice_model_path "RVC/TTS model path"
        float formant_shift "formant frequency adjustment"
        int whisper_mode "0 or 1"
        float reverb_wetness "reverb blend 0.0 - 1.0"
        datetime created_at
    }

    SPEECH_MODULATION_LOGS {
        string log_id PK
        string message_id FK
        string profile_id FK
        string input_audio_path
        string output_audio_path
        int modulation_duration_ms
        string additional_metadata "JSON extra metadata"
        datetime created_at
    }
```

